.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Hidden-pool probes must NEVER be committed to this PUBLIC repo. The real boundary is a
# separate PRIVATE fuzz-catalog repo (see FUZZ_RUNNER_SPEC.md); this is only a backstop.
**/hidden/
catalog-hidden/

# GRADING OUTPUT MUST NOT BE PUBLISHED. A results file names real third-party apps and carries,
# per finding, a paste-to-reproduce request against a live deployment — the v9/v10 corpus runs alone
# held 1,709 named Devpost projects and 8,825 repro blocks. Black-box scanning of a public URL is one
# thing; publishing per-app reproduction steps against somebody else's submission is a different act,
# and it contradicts the product's own guardrail (hand the builder back a private report, upside-only).
#
# These landed here because the league->mirror sync is `rsync` followed by `git add -A`: rsync copies
# the untracked results across and add -A stages whatever it finds. The sync command now carries
# matching --exclude flags, and this file is the backstop for when someone forgets one.
*.jsonl
*.log
*.tsv
v9-baseline-stats.json
nextjs-trace-sample.txt
sprint-sample.txt
terminal output of test.md
